tatus="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI SHUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAURA JUNICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NITTA, YOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIRANE, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, SHUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAURA, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A non-aqueous electrolyte secondary cell in which the positive plate is made of a lithium-containing composite oxide capable of absorbing/releasing lithium and the negative plate is made of a compound having a large irreversibility capacity and a lithium-containing composite nitride. The non-aqueous electrolyte secondary cell is characterized in that the negative plate is made of a metal oxide and a lithium-containing composite nitride expressed by the general formula: Li3-XMXN (M is a transition metal and X is 0.2&lt;X&lt;/=0.8). The transition metal M is preferably cobalt (Co) because such a lithium-containing compound nitride has a large capacity and is excellent in reversibility. The material of the positive plate can be a lithium-containing composite nitride represented by lithium cobaltate, lithium nickelate, a composite compound of lithium nickelate, or a lithium manganesate (LiMn2O4). By adding a lithium-containing composite nitride in the negative plate, the non-aqueous electrolyte secondary cell has a large capacity, an excellent cycle reversibility, and a high quality.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un accumulateur à électrolyte non aqueux dont la plaque positive est faite d'un oxyde composite au lithium capable d'absorber et de libérer du lithium, et la plaque négative, d'un composé à forte capacité d'irréversibilité et d'un nitrure composite au lithium. La plaque négative est faite d'un oxyde métallique et d'un nitrure composite de formule générale Li3-XMXN (M étant un métal de transition et X étant 0,2 &lt; X &lt;/= 0,8). Le métal M est de préférence du cobalt (Co) car un tel nitrure composite au lithium présente une forte capacité et une excellente réversibilité. Le matériau de la plaque positive peut être un nitrure composite au lithium tel que du cobaltate de lithium, du nickelate de lithium, un composé composite de nickelate de lithium, ou un manganésate de lithium (LiMn2O4). Cette adjonction de nitrure composite à la plaque négative donne un accumulateur de qualité élevée, à forte capacité et excellente réversibilité du cycle.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>